  "text": "__)\n\n\nTo find the area of triangle \\( \\triangle BGE \\), we need to determine the coordinates of points \\( B, G, \\) and \\( E \\). Let's assume point \\( A \\) is at the origin \\((0, 0)\\). Since points \\( B, C, D, E, \\) and \\( F \\) lie on a straight line, we can denote their coordinates as follows:\n- \\( B = (x_1, 0) \\)\n- \\( C = (x_2, 0) \\)\n- \\( D = (x_3, 0) \\)\n- \\( E = (x_4, 0) \\)\n- \\( F = (x_5, 0) \\)\n\nGiven the distances, we can write the following equations:\n- \\( AC = 26 \\) implies \\( x_2 - 0 = 26 \\), so \\( x_2 = 26 \\)\n- \\( BD = 22 \\) implies \\( x_3 - x_1 = 22 \\)\n- \\( CE = 31 \\) implies \\( x_4 - x_2 = 31 \\)\n- \\( DF = 33 \\) implies \\( x_5 - x_3 = 33 \\)\n- \\( AF = 73 \\) implies \\( x_5 - 0 = 73 \\), so \\( x_5 = 73 \\)\n\nFrom \\( x_5 - x_3 = 33 \\), we get \\( 73 - x_3 = 33 \\), so \\( x_3 = 40 \\). From \\( x_3 - x_1 = 22 \\), we get \\( 40 - x_1 = 22 \\), so \\( x_1 = 18 \\). From \\( x_4 - x_2 = 31 \\), we get \\( x_4 - 26 = 31 \\), so \\( x_4 = 57 \\).\n\nNow we know the coordinates of all points:\n- \\( A = (0, 0) \\)\n- \\( B = (18, 0) \\)\n- \\( C = (26, 0) \\)\n- \\( D = (40, 0) \\)\n- \\( E = (57, 0) \\)\n- \\( F = (73, 0) \\)\n\nSince \\( G \\) is not on the line, let's denote its coordinates as \\( (x_G, y_G) \\). We know the following distances:\n- \\( CG = 40 \\) implies \\( x_G - 26 = 40 \\), so \\( x_G = 66 \\)\n- \\( DG = 30 \\) implies \\( y_G = 30 \\)\n\nThus, \\( G = (66, 30) \\).\n\nNow we need to find the area of \\( \\triangle BGE \\). The vertices of \\( \\triangle BGE \\) are \\( B = (18, 0) \\), \\( G = (66, 30) \\), and \\( E = (57, 0) \\). The area of a triangle with vertices \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\]\nSubstituting the coordinates of \\( B, G, \\) and \\( E \\):\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 18(30 - 0) + 66(0 - 0) + 57(0 - 30) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 18 \\cdot 30 + 57 \\cdot (-30) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 540 - 1710 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -1170 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1170 = 585\n\\]\nThus, the area of \\( \\triangle BGE \\) is \\(\\boxed{585}\\).",
